11
00:03:03,381 --> 00:03:19,984
MAYA: So we're trading on the *hope* that something *might* happen, and nobody's actually hedging for the scenario where negotiations stall? That seems structurally sound. What happens to oil if the White House comes back and says the deal didn't work out?
  ↳ source: https://www.axios.com/2026/05/24/iran-deal-white-house-delay-days-trump

12
00:03:19,984 --> 00:03:38,096
ALEX: Crude jumps in the opposite direction, Merck tanks back down to where it was yesterday, and we all collectively pretend the past forty-eight hours didn't happen. If talks collapse, you're looking at energy stocks repricing. Energy stocks are currently priced for peace. They're not hedged for chaos.

13
00:03:38,096 --> 00:03:57,717
